WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:02.500
Good evening.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:03.840
Hope you had a nice day.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.300
Let's have a look at our chart and see how things went.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.230
Quite a mixed bag, as you can see today.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.370
Caused mostly by this coal front up here in the Gulf,

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.450
moving down through the Kimberleys,

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.080
across the Great Divide, and over to the coast.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.480
Also affecting our chart was this thigh pressure,

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.970
just below Tasmania.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.040
which should move north tomorrow

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.600
and settle somewhere about here

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.680
over surface paradise.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.390
Oh, the temperature today was pretty widespread,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.770
topped with a maximum of 37

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.050
up here at Mount Pleasant,

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.640
and going all the way down to a low of 14

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.180
down here at Perisher Valley.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.910
Oh, incidentally, there was a little drizzle

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.860
reported earlier up here, just below the bite.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.580
Let's expect it to clear up soon.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:00:59.970
All right, so much...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.050
for today's lovely weather let's have a look now and see what tomorrow has in store for us

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:18.980
doesn't look very promising does it all in all a pretty daggy day tomorrow
